<title>UK: Whitbread to open 35 more Costa Coffee shops.</title>
<headline>Whitbread to open 35 more Costa Coffee shops.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewer-to-leisure group Whitbread Plc said on Monday it planned to open 35 new Costa Coffee stores in Britain by early 1998.</p>
<p>The expansion plan would create over 300 new jobs, taking the total for the division to about 700 and about 90 outlets, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Costa will also take some six airport concessions currently operating as Steff's Cafes at Stansted, Gatwick and Heathrow airports.</p>
<p>Mike Dowell, managing director of Costa, said: &quot;Costa's expansion is a result of the ever growing demand for real coffee in the UK. The total coffee market has seen value growth of 19 percent in current terms over the 1991-1995 period and Whitbread estimates that demand for real coffee will grow by over 60 percent by the year 2001.&quot;</p>
<p>- Tim Farrand, London newsroom +44 171 542 6437</p>
